<section class="truth-hero"><div class="truth-hero__copy" data-reveal><span class="pub-kicker"><i></i> AI-powered inventory &amp; operations</span><h1>Let StockChief run the routine.<br><em>Keep the decisions.</em></h1><p>StockChief works across stock, orders, purchasing and Money. It prepares and carries out supported work under your authority, and brings questions, approvals and exceptions back to you.</p><div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-btn" href="/demo">Watch StockChief work ↗</a><a class="pub-text-link" href="/pricing">Find your plan →</a></div><p class="truth-proof">Your records. Your connected accounts. Your approval rules.</p></div><figure class="truth-product" data-reveal><div class="truth-product__bar"><span class="truth-dot"></span> The actual StockChief application <span>Demo business</span></div><img src="/demo/inventory.png?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" alt="StockChief’s real item page showing stock by location and supporting records" fetchpriority="high" width="1440" height="900"><figcaption>Captured in a reproducible demonstration business.</figcaption><a href="/demo" class="truth-product__play" aria-label="Watch the real product walkthrough">▶ See it in action</a></figure></section>
<section class="truth-operation" aria-label="One connected operation"><span>Orders</span><i>→</i><span>Stock</span><i>→</i><span>Purchasing</span><i>→</i><span>Fulfillment</span><i>→</i><span>Money</span></section>
<section class="truth-section" data-reveal><div><p class="pub-kicker">See the work, not a promise</p><h2>Real screens.<br>A connected way to work.</h2><p>Follow stock across locations, review a purchase order and ask a question grounded in the same records.</p><a class="pub-text-link" href="/demo">Watch the guided product demonstration →</a></div><div class="truth-steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Know what is available</h3><p>See on-hand, available and incoming stock, with movement history that explains the balance.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Prepare the next move</h3><p>Review replenishment and purchasing using recorded stock, demand and supplier terms.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Keep the consequences together</h3><p>Physical receiving, fulfillment, invoices and payments retain their own evidence and approval steps.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section class="truth-feature-grid"><article class="truth-feature truth-feature--wide" data-reveal><div><p class="pub-kicker">Stock that makes sense</p><h2>One product.<br>Every place it matters.</h2><p>Products, variants, SKUs and locations. Track quantities, lots and serials using the workflows your inventory needs.</p><a class="pub-text-link" href="/capabilities">Explore stock and operations →</a></div><figure><img loading="lazy" src="/demo/inventory.png?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" alt="Actual inventory screen in the controlled demonstration business" width="1440" height="900"></figure></article><article class="truth-feature" data-reveal><p class="pub-kicker">Buy with context</p><h2>See what is coming.<br>Plan what comes next.</h2><p>Supplier items, purchase orders, expected deliveries and receipts stay connected. A supplier invoice never silently receives physical goods.</p><figure><img loading="lazy" src="/demo/purchasing.png?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" alt="Actual purchase order separating ordered quantities from receiving and billing" width="1440" height="900"></figure></article><article class="truth-feature" data-reveal><p class="pub-kicker">Ask StockChief</p><h2>Questions become<br>a useful next step.</h2><p>Read business records, investigate issues, prepare supported workflows and build reports. Stock and financial changes follow your authority and approvals.</p><figure><img loading="lazy" src="/demo/ask.png?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" alt="An actual StockChief answer grounded in demonstration inventory" width="1440" height="900"></figure></article></section>
<section class="truth-section" data-reveal><div><p class="pub-kicker">Needs you</p><h2>Keep your attention<br>on the decisions.</h2><p>Missing facts, approvals and operational issues have a place to be reviewed. Inspect the supporting records before allowing a change.</p><a class="pub-text-link" href="/control">Understand approvals and control →</a></div><figure class="truth-screen"><img loading="lazy" src="/demo/brief.png?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" alt="Actual StockChief Home screen with demonstration business activity" width="1440" height="900"><figcaption>The current application, captured with synthetic demo records.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="truth-connections" data-reveal><p class="pub-kicker">Bring your systems together</p><h2>Use the accounts<br>you already work with.</h2><p>Connect supported stores, mailboxes, accounting companies, payment and shipping accounts. Available actions depend on the provider, permissions, plan and setup.</p><div class="truth-provider-row"><% for(const group of groups){for(const provider of group.providers){ %><a href="/integrations#group-<%= group.title.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-') %>"><% if(provider.logo){ %><img loading="lazy" src="/provider-logos/<%= provider.logo %>.svg" alt="" width="28" height="28"><% } %><span><%= provider.name %></span></a><% }} %></div><a class="pub-text-link" href="/integrations">Explore connections and supported work →</a></section>
<section class="truth-section" data-reveal><div><p class="pub-kicker">Move with confidence</p><h2>Start with the records<br>you already have.</h2><p>Bring a spreadsheet, document, readable image or supported connected system. Review the interpretation, corrections and required questions before approving an import.</p><p>Unreadable or incomplete evidence needs clarification. StockChief preserves what it can read and shows what still needs a decision.</p><a class="pub-text-link" href="/switching">See how importing works →</a></div><div class="truth-switch__steps"><span>Upload or connect</span><i>↓</i><span>Review fields and questions</span><i>↓</i><span>Approve and verify</span></div></section>
